      "end": 5.117,
      "startFrame": 112,
      "endFrame": 154,
      "words": 4,
      "text": "And you wouldn't notice."
    },
    {
      "i": 2,
      "start": 5.277,
      "end": 8.563,
      "startFrame": 158,
      "endFrame": 257,
      "words": 8,
      "text": "All day, a sleepy signal builds up: adenosine."
    },
    {
      "i": 3,
      "start": 8.723,
      "end": 11.731,
      "startFrame": 262,
      "endFrame": 352,
      "words": 9,
      "text": "Caffeine plugs its receptors, so you don't feel it."
    },
    {
      "i": 4,
      "start": 11.891,
      "end": 14.963,
      "startFrame": 357,
      "endFrame": 449,
      "words": 8,
      "text": "The catch: caffeine's half-life is about four hours."
    },
    {
      "i": 5,
      "start": 15.123,
      "end": 17.661,
      "startFrame": 454,
      "endFrame": 530,
      "words": 8,
      "text": "For some people it's two. For others, eight."
    },
    {
      "i": 6,
      "start": 17.821,
      "end": 20.275,
      "startFrame": 535,
      "endFrame": 608,
      "words": 11,
      "text": "So part of that cup is still in you at bedtime."
    },
    {
      "i": 7,
      "start": 20.435,
      "end": 24.104,
      "startFrame": 613,
      "endFrame": 723,
      "words": 10,
      "text": "In a small study, twelve people took four hundred milligrams"
